---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site";

const { controller, contact, updated } = site.privacy;
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy Notice | ${site.name}`}
  description={`How ${controller} handles personal data on ${site.url.replace("https://", "")}.`}
  heading="Privacy"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="meta caps-label">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website is run by <strong>{controller}</strong>, which is the data controller for personal data collected
      here. Questions or requests about your data: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Newsletter and SMS</h2>
    <p>When you sign up to updates from {site.name} we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your email address</li>
      <li>your phone number, if you choose to give it (optional, for SMS)</li>
      <li>your country and approximate location, derived from your IP address</li>
      <li>your IP address and the time you signed up</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use this to send you news about {site.name} by email and, if you gave your number, by SMS, and to send the right
      news to the right countries. The legal basis is your consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it at any time
      with the unsubscribe link in every email, by replying STOP to an SMS, or by emailing us.
    </p>
    <p>We keep this data until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it.</p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      If you accept cookies, we use Google Analytics to understand how the site is used, such as visits, where visitors
      come from and which links they click. It sets the cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, which last up to
      two years. If you decline, Google Analytics is not loaded and no cookies are set. We store your choice in your
      browser's local storage so we don't ask again.
    </p>
    <p>The legal basis is your consent. Analytics data is kept for up to 14 months.</p>
    <p><button type="button" class="button primary" data-cookie-settings>Change cookie settings</button></p>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>We use these providers to run the site. They process data on our behalf under data processing agreements:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Mailchimp</strong> (Intuit Inc., USA): email and SMS sending, subscriber list</li>
      <li><strong>Netlify</strong> (Netlify Inc., USA): website hosting and signup handling</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (Google Ireland Ltd / Google LLC): analytics, only with your consent</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Some of this data is transferred to the USA. These transfers rely on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework and the EU
      Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, correct or delete your data, to restrict or object to its use, to get a copy of it,
      and to withdraw your consent at any time. Email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> and we will reply within
      one month.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you think we handle your data wrongly, you can complain to the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (IMY),
      <a href="https://www.imy.se" target="_blank" rel="noopener">imy.se</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="back"><a href="/" class="caps-label">Back to {site.name}</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    background: #000000b3;
    padding: 24px 20px;
  }
  .meta {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 28px 0 8px;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--caps-tracking);
  }
  p,
  ul {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 18px;
  }
  a {
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .button {
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .back {
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }
  .back a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
